  "query_preview": ".. Subsidence behind the front will usher in surface high\npressure late on Thursday, which should stick around for the \nbetter part of the extended. As such, expect a pattern shift to\ncooler and drier weather, with the exception of 20 to 30% chance\nof rain on Saturday. With surface high sitting overhead and\nfalling temperatures, conditions should be favorable for effective\nradiational cooling and frost development at times during the\nearly morning periods throughout the week. Will continue to\nmonitor trends for headline potential as we approach the end of\nthe growing season.",
